TEXT 96 -80 Left 3 ;#417 Alan's manual transition-frequency test circuit
TEXT 96 -16 Left 2 ;Source: Alan Wolke (W2AEW), https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PRzytyqwK5U
TEXT 96 32 Left 2 ;A fixed bias holds 10 mA of collector current while a small signal drives the base through 560 ohm. The ratio of the two current amplitudes is the gain at that frequency.
TEXT 96 600 Left 2 !.step param FREQ list 300k 3Meg
TEXT 96 640 Left 2 !.tran 0 110u 0 2n
TEXT 96 680 Left 2 !.meas tran IC_DC AVG I(Vcprobe) FROM {20/FREQ} TO {30/FREQ}
TEXT 96 720 Left 2 !.meas tran IB_DC AVG I(Rb) FROM {20/FREQ} TO {30/FREQ}
TEXT 96 760 Left 2 !.meas tran IC_AMP PP I(Vcprobe) FROM {20/FREQ} TO {30/FREQ}
TEXT 96 800 Left 2 !.meas tran IB_AMP PP I(Rb) FROM {20/FREQ} TO {30/FREQ}
TEXT 96 840 Left 2 !.meas tran HFE PARAM IC_AMP/IB_AMP
TEXT 96 880 Left 2 !.meas tran FT PARAM FREQ*IC_AMP/IB_AMP
TEXT 96 920 Left 2 !.save I(Vcprobe) I(Rb)
TEXT 96 984 Left 2 ;VCPROBE is a zero-volt source standing for the TCP0030 current probe Alan clamps on the collector lead, so I(Vcprobe) is his CH1.
TEXT 96 1024 Left 2 ;I(Rb) is his CH2: he reads the base current as the voltage his TDP4000 differential probe sees across the 560 ohm, scaled to microamps.
TEXT 96 1064 Left 2 ;RSRC, RA1, RA2, RA3 and RTERM are the generator source impedance and the 5x 50 ohm attenuator pad he draws as a box. V1 carries his 100 mV peak to peak setting.
TEXT 96 1104 Left 2 ;VBIAS is not shown in the video; 6.51 V is the value that puts the collector current at the 10 mA his scope measures. CBLOCK is his DC block, value not shown.
TEXT 96 1144 Left 2 ;Q1 is a 2N2222. The device in the video is identified only as an NPN silicon BJT with hFE = 198 on his DCA75, so this is a stand-in with a similar low-frequency gain.
